<?xml version="1.0" encoding="windows-1252"?>
<Module xmlns="http://waters.sourceforge.net/xsd/module" xmlns:B="http://waters.sourceforge.net/xsd/base" Name="NineGameAbstractP2win">
<B:Comment>Abstract version of the NineGame.
This version is from P2's perspective, that is p2's events are controllable and p1's are uncontrollable, and state P1 is marked
There is no winning strategy for P2 (if P1 plays perfectly, that is, start by choosing 1)

But, if P1 does not play perfectly, meaning P1 starts by selecting 2 or 3, then there does exist a winning strategy for P2.
That is shown in this model.</B:Comment>
